While treating a patient for cardiac rehab, a physical therapist relies on the Borg rating of perceived exertion (RPE) scale. The Borg RPE scale is MOST representative of which type of data scale?
A.  Nominal
B. Ordinal
C. Cardinal
D. Marginal

The correct answer is B:
A.  Nominal scales are used to indicate categories that are not higher or lower (example: race, gender, etc.)
B.  Ordinal scales are used to represent data that is comparatively higher or lower that other data. This is the most correct answer.
C.  Cardinal scales are used when there is an absolute zero and are quantitative. Age and weight are good examples of these.
D.  Not related.
